Clearly  $3^{2012}\equiv 1 \pmod{5}$ , hence  $Q(3^{2012})\equiv Q(1)=P(1) \equiv P(16) \equiv 1 \pmod{5},$  hence  $|Q(3^{2012})| \ge 1.$ Now, let  $P(x)=ax^2+bx+c$  and  $Q(x)=cx^2+ax+b$ . We are asked to solve the system

\begin{align*}
a*16^2+b*16+c &= 3^{2012} 
c*(3^{2012})^2+a*3^{2012}+b &= 1
\end{align*}

Substituting for  $c$  in the second equation yields
\begin{align*}
(3^{2012})^2(3^{2012}-a*16^2-b*16)+a*3^{2012}+b &=1 
\end{align*}
