Since 4 has the positive divisors 1, 2, and 4, these can be checked against the LHS factors in (ii): $a(a+1) + N = 4, a(a+1) - N = 1 \Rightarrow 2a(a+1) = 5$  (a contradiction & can be eliminated); $a(a+1) + N = 2, a(a+1) - N = 2 \Rightarrow 2a(a+1) = 4 \Rightarrow  a(a+1) = 2  \Rightarrow  a^2 + a - 2 = (a+2)(a-1) = 0  \Rightarrow  a = -2, 1$  and  $N = 0$ .

