Then \begin{align*} \sum_{n=1}^{2^k} S_2(n) & = \left(\sum_{n=1}^k \sum_{m=1}^n m g(n,m) \right) + 1  & = \left( \sum_{n=1}^k \sum_{m=1}^n m \binom{ n-1}{m-1} \right) + 1 
& = \left( \sum_{n=1}^k (n+1)2^{n-2} \right) + 1  & = 2^{k-1}k + 1 \end{align*}

